 "metadata": {
  "title": "NGS Mount Everest AWS Network",
  "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21666973",
  "publication_date": "2026-07-29",
  "description": "<p>The Automatic Weather Stations (AWSs) in the Khumbu Valley were installed during the <span><span>National Geographic Society</span></span> Perpetual Planet Everest Expedition between 2019 and 2022. A total of six AWSs were deployed at elevations ranging from 3,810 m to 8,810 m above sea level and have been regularly maintained since installation.</p>",
